{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' .ralph/projects/tank-sim/loops/005-substrate-nutrient-dynamics-plant-growth-and/20260315053040-spec.md\"","aggregated_output":"---\nartifact: spec\nloop: 5\nproject: tank-sim\nbackend: claude(opus)\nrole: planner\ncreated_at: 2026-03-15T05:30:40Z\n---\n\nI now have a complete picture. Here is the feature specification for Loop 5:\n\n# Feature: Substrate Nutrient Dynamics, Plant Growth, and Algae/Periphyton Competition\n\n## Description\nActivate the currently inert plant guilds, substrate nutrient stores, and algae/periphyton pools by implementing daily growth kinetics, nutrient uptake pathways, and competition mechanics. After this loop, plants grow or decline based on light, temperature, and nutrient availability (water-column vs substrate depending on guild); algae and periphyton compete with plants for light and dissolved nutrients; substrate nutrient stores are consumed by rooted plants; and dying biomass enters the detritus pathway. This corresponds to milestone 5 in the master prompt.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] **Daily plant growth** — each plant guild updates biomass daily using: `net_growth = biomass * max_rate * f_light * f_temp * min(f_n, f_p, f_c) * habitat_factor * (1 - crowding) - respiration - senescence`\n- [ ] **Guild-differentiated nutrient uptake** — `FastStem` draws N and P primarily from the water column (`water_column_uptake_bias = 0.9`); `RootFeedingRosette` draws primarily from substrate stores (`substrate_uptake_bias = 0.9`). Uptake removes mass from `ammonia_total_mg_n_total` / `nitrate_mg_n_total` / `phosphate_mg_p_total` (water column) or `nutrient_store_mg_n_total` / `nutrient_store_mg_p_total` (substrate layers).\n- [ ] **Substrate nutrient depletion** — rooted plant uptake reduces substrate N and P stores over time; active planted substrate starts with higher stores than inert substrate and supports better rosette growth.\n- [ ] **Plant crowding and self-shading** — `crowding_index` is recomputed daily based on total plant biomass relative to tank surface area; higher crowding reduces growth and shades algae.\n- [ ] **Plant habitat factor** — `habitat_index` for `RootFeedingRosette` depends on substrate depth and CEC; `FastStem` gets a flat high habitat factor regardless of substrate.\n- [ ] **Plant health tracking** — `health_index` degrades under persistent nutrient deficiency or poor light; recovers slowly when conditions improve.\n- [ ] **Senescence to detritus** — a fraction of plant biomass lost to senescence and trimming enters `fine_detritus_g_total`.\n- [ ] **Daily algae growth** — suspended algae and periphyton grow based on light, temperature, dissolved N and P, reduced by plant shading (crowding) and microfauna grazing.\n- [ ] **Periphyton surface limitation** — periphyton growth is capped by total colonizable area from substrate layers plus wall area.\n- [ ] **Nuisance index update** — `nuisance_index` recalculated daily from combined algae + periphyton pressure relative to tank size.\n- [ ] **Algae event emission** — `AlgaeRiskRising` emitted when nuisance index crosses 0.5; `AlgaeBloom` emitted when suspended algae biomass exceeds a threshold per liter.\n- [ ] **Plant process parameters** — new fields added to `ProcessParams` for plant max growth rate, respiration fraction, senescence fraction, nutrient half-saturation constants, light and temperature response curves, and algae growth parameters.\n- [ ] **Snapshot exposure** — `TankSnapshot` extended with `suspended_algae_biomass_g`, `periphyton_biomass_g`, `algae_nuisance_index`, per-guild plant biomass summaries, and substrate nutrient remaining.\n- [ ] **Acceptance test: `rooted_substrate_advantage`** — same `RootFeedingRosette` in active substrate vs inert sand; after 30 days biomass in active substrate is at least 15% higher.\n- [ ] **Acceptance test: `overfeeding_effects` (algae component)** — overfed tank after 14 days has higher algae nuisance index than control.\n- [ ] **Integration with hourly DO/DIC pipeline** — photosynthesis and respiration rates already use `photosynthetic_biomass_g()` and `respiring_biomass_g()`, which read current plant/algae biomass; as biomass grows or declines daily, these hourly effects automatically scale. No hourly pipeline change needed for this coupling.\n- [ ] **TrimPlants action produces detritus** — trimmed plant mass enters `fine_detritus_g_total` instead of vanishing.\n- [ ] **Invariants hold** — plant biomass, algae biomass, substrate nutrients, health/crowding/habitat indices all satisfy existing invariant checks (non-negative, 0..1 for indices).\n\n## Files to Modify/Create\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/plant_growth.rs` — **NEW**: daily plant growth system with guild-specific nutrient uptake, crowding, habitat, senescence, and health update\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/algae_growth.rs` — **NEW**: daily algae and periphyton growth with nutrient competition, surface limitation, and nuisance index\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/mod.rs` — register `plant_growth` and `algae_growth` modules\n- `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs` — wire `plant_growth::step_daily_plants()` and `algae_growth::step_daily_algae()` into `run_daily_update()`; update `TrimPlants` action to route trimmed mass to detritus\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs` — add plant growth kinetics parameters (max growth rates per guild, respiration fraction, senescence fraction, N/P/C half-saturation, light/temp response coefficients, algae growth rate, periphyton cap scaling)\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs` — extend `TankSnapshot` with algae biomass fields, per-guild summaries, substrate nutrient totals\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs` — no structural changes needed (existing types are sufficient), but may add a helper method for computing total colonizable area across substrate layers\n- `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs` — add non-negative check for `algae.suspended_biomass_g` and `algae.periphyton_biomass_g` (currently unchecked)\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/events.rs` — add daily algae threshold events (`AlgaeRiskRising`, `AlgaeBloom`, `SubstrateFoulingWarning`)\n- `crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml` — add default values for new plant/algae process parameters\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/rooted_substrate_advantage.rs` — **NEW**: acceptance test #8\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/plant_algae_integration.rs` — **NEW**: tests for plant growth under varying light/nutrients, algae bloom conditions, guild differentiation, and trim-to-detritus\n\n## Dependencies\n- Requires: Loop 4 (detritus/mineralization pipeline — plants must route senescence to detritus, and mineralized nutrients feed back to plant uptake)\n- Blocks: Loop 6 (shrimp population — shrimp condition depends on periphyton as food source, and plant health affects habitat quality)\n\n---\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
