{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' .ralph/projects/tank-sim/loops/005-substrate-nutrient-dynamics-plant-growth-and/20260315054215-impl-notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"---\nartifact: impl-notes\nloop: 5\nproject: tank-sim\nbackend: codex(gpt-5.4-high)\nrole: implementer\ncreated_at: 2026-03-15T05:42:15Z\n---\n\nI’m implementing loop 5 in `tank_core`, starting by reading the existing biology/types/engine/test structure so the new plant and algae systems fit the current update pipeline and invariants.\nI’ve mapped the existing daily/hourly hooks and the relevant state surfaces. Next I’m reading the core type definitions and current engine behavior so I can add the new systems without fighting the current model.\nThe current state is simple enough that this can stay additive: new daily systems, extra process fields, extended snapshot, and a small action fix. I’m reading the preset loader and a few system utilities now to match naming and avoid breaking scenario loading.\nI found the scenario conversion layer too, which matters because new process fields need to survive preset loading. Next I’m reading that conversion and then I’ll patch the types and daily systems in one pass.\nI have enough context to make the main changes. Plan is:\n1. Extend types and preset conversion for plant/algae parameters and new snapshot data.\n2. Add `plant_growth` and `algae_growth` daily systems plus event hooks.\n3. Wire daily execution and trim-to-detritus in the engine, then tighten invariants.\n4. Add acceptance/integration tests and run the full relevant build/test cycle, fixing anything that breaks.\nThe shell path here doesn’t include `cargo`, so I’m locating the toolchain explicitly before running verification. The code changes themselves can proceed normally.\nI’m at the edit phase now. The first patch extends the core process/state surfaces so the new daily systems have stable parameters and observability to write against.\nI found one existing coupling hole while wiring this: hourly photosynthesis already scales from “photosynthetic biomass”, but it was excluding suspended algae. I’m correcting that alongside the new daily biomass systems so the intended loop-5 coupling is real.\nI’ve wired the core engine path. The remaining structural work is the data layer: process preset schema, scenario conversion, and tests. After that I can run the compiler and tighten any borrow/type issues.\nI’m adding the acceptance and integration tests now. They’re targeted at the new daily behavior, not just the new fields, so they should catch most regressions in the plant/algae loop.\nI caught one test issue before compile: `TrimPlants` detritus is added at tick start, and the hourly detritus pipeline would immediately dissolve some of it. I’m zeroing that rate in the trim test so it measures only the action behavior.\nThe toolchain is available through `nix shell`, so I’m formatting and then running the workspace checks/tests under that shell rather than relying on the ambient PATH.\nThe first compile pass is running now. I’ve already cleared one environment blocker by adding a linker; next step is to fix the actual Rust errors that come back from the workspace build.\nThe only failing test is the bloom threshold setup, not the implementation path. The default tank volume is larger than I estimated, so I’m correcting the test fixture to exceed the configured `g/L` bloom threshold on the actual geometry.\nThe workspace now builds cleanly and the full test suite passes under `nix shell ... cargo test --workspace`. I’m doing one last pass over the diff to summarize the behavior-level changes and note any deliberate tradeoffs.\n`cargo fmt --all` widened the diff into a handful of files I didn’t functionally change. I’m checking those now so I can either keep only meaningful edits or call out the remaining formatting/build-artifact noise accurately.\nI’m shrinking the diff before I finish. There are two kinds of noise I don’t want to leave behind: tracked `target/` build outputs from verification, and pure formatting churn in files I didn’t otherwise touch.\n# Implementation Notes\n\n## Decisions Made\n- Added daily `plant_growth` and `algae_growth` systems and wired them into `run_daily_update()`, so plant/algae biomass now changes once per day while existing hourly DO/DIC coupling scales automatically from current biomass.\n- Implemented guild-specific nutrient uptake biases with `FastStem` favoring water-column N/P and `RootFeedingRosette` favoring substrate stores, plus daily crowding, habitat, senescence, and health updates.\n- Extended `ProcessParams`, preset loading, and scenario conversion with plant/algae growth parameters so the new behavior is configurable and deterministic from saved state/presets.\n- Extended `TankSnapshot` with algae biomass, nuisance index, per-guild plant biomass, and remaining substrate nutrients for TUI/API observability.\n- Updated algae event emission to cover `AlgaeRiskRising`, `AlgaeBloom`, and `SubstrateFoulingWarning`, and changed `TrimPlants` so trimmed biomass enters `fine_detritus_g_total`.\n- Added acceptance/integration coverage for rooted substrate advantage, plant response to light/nutrients, uptake differentiation, algae bloom/overfeeding behavior, and trim-to-detritus routing.\n\n## Spec Deviations\n- None.\n\n## Testing\n- Verified with `nix shell nixpkgs#cargo nixpkgs#rustc nixpkgs#gcc -c cargo test --workspace`.\n- New acceptance tests: `rooted_substrate_advantage` and `plant_algae_integration`.\n- Verification created untracked build artifacts under `target/` and an untracked log under `.ralph/tmp/logs/`.\n\n---\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
